{"kind": "opendata", "id": "australia:coral-sea-marine-park-coral-reef-health-survey-2023", "name": "Coral Sea Marine Park Coral Reef Health Survey 2023", "organization": "Parks Australia", "source": null, "notes": "Coral reef health assessments were undertaken across the central and northern Coral Sea Marine Park during a 31-day voyage from February to March 2023. Surveys were conducted across 48 sites at 11 reef systems, including Flinders, Diamond, Lihou, Willis, Moore and Holmes Reefs, Herald Cays, and Bougainville, Osprey, Ashmore and Boot Reefs. The assessments formed part of ongoing monitoring of coral reef ecosystems within the Coral Sea Marine Park and were undertaken by James Cook University for…", "tags": ["Coral Sea", "Coral Sea Marine Park", "australian marine parks", "coral bleaching", "coral cover", "coral reef health", "coral reefs", "marine biodiversity"], "formats": ["PDF", "word"], "countries": ["Australia"], "year_start": 2023, "year_end": 2023, "frequency": null, "update_frequency": null, "year_label": "years"}
