{"kind": "opendata", "id": "zenodo:17161438", "name": "Malawi Malaria Incidence 2005-2023", "organization": "Zenodo", "source": "Maxwell T. Elling; Karnauskas, Kris; Kowalcyk, Megan; Mategula, Donnie; Chirombo, James; Livneh, Ben; McCann, Robert; B…", "notes": "Monthly malaria case data reported at the district level across Malawi. See Elling et al., 2026 for more information. Citation: Elling, M.T., Karnauskas, K.B., Kowalcyk, M. et al. Tropical oceans drive variability in soil moisture and malaria in Malawi. Commun Med (2026). https://doi.org/10.1038/s43856-026-01681-9", "tags": [], "formats": ["CSV"], "countries": ["Malawi"], "year_start": 2025, "year_end": 2025, "year_label": "publication year", "frequency": null, "update_frequency": null}
{"kind": "opendata", "id": "zenodo:14756245", "name": "IMPROVE Anti-inflammatory effects of sulphadoxine-pyrimethamine for intermittent preventive treatment for malaria in pregnancy (GHDC-SI-ID-45)", "organization": "Zenodo", "source": "ter Kuile, Feiko; Obermoser, Gerlinde", "notes": "The Improving PRegnancy Outcomes With Intermittent preVEntive Treatment in Africa (IMPROVE) study is a 3-arm malaria chemoprevention trial with monthly intermittent preventive treatment in pregnancy, or IPTp, in Malawi, Kenya and Tanzania (Clinicaltrials.gov: NCT03208179Trial ). Using Olink, we profiled plasma cytokine levels in pregnant women at enrolment, around 28 weeks and 36 weeks (or delivery) at Stanford's Human Immune Monitorin Center (HIMC).", "tags": [], "formats": [], "countries": ["Kenya", "Malawi", "Tanzania"], "year_start": 2025, "year_end": 2025, "year_label": "publication year", "frequency": null, "update_frequency": null}
