{"kind": "opendata", "id": "zenodo:13983147", "name": "Simulated datasets from  modelling demographic events and migration patterns", "organization": "Zenodo", "source": "Evans, Omondi", "notes": "These are datasets generated from multi-state model (MSM) project on understanding demographic events and migration patterns in two urban slums of Nairobi City in Kenya at the African Population and Health Research Center (APHRC). The project focuses on using MSM techniques to analyze residence demographic events in Nairobi urban slums, with an emphasis on key events such as: Births Deaths Migration (in-migration and out-migration) Changes in residence status (exit and entry) The primary aim of…", "tags": ["Population", "Urban slums", "Migration", "Surveillance", "Multi-state model"], "formats": ["RDATA"], "countries": ["Kenya"], "year_start": 2024, "year_end": 2024, "year_label": "publication year", "frequency": null, "update_frequency": null}
{"kind": "opendata", "id": "zenodo:19643626", "name": "Social, Economic, and Environmental Benefits of Vernacular Architecture in Post-Disaster Reconstruction", "organization": "Zenodo", "source": "Fawzya Ewiss; HAJISMAIL, SALAH", "notes": "The ongoing process of rebuilding after a disaster has some ongoing challenges with regard to social acceptability, economic viability, and environmental sustainability. The majority of reconstruction programs utilize standardized housing models that may not adequately address local culture, available economic means, and environmental factors. Therefore, the transition from temporary housing to long-term settlement is often not resilient and does not provide residents with a satisfactory soluti…", "tags": ["Post-Disaster Reconstruction", "Vernacular Architecture", "Sustainability", "Community Resilience", "Housing Recovery"], "formats": ["PDF"], "countries": ["Haiti", "Sri Lanka", "Syrian Arab Republic"], "year_start": 2026, "year_end": 2026, "year_label": "publication year", "frequency": null, "update_frequency": null}
